    "created_at": "2024-03-19T14:21:49Z",
    "updated_at": "2024-03-19T14:21:49Z",
    "body": "So recall that `shadowroot` was renamed to `shadowrootmode` precisely and only to make room for the IDL `shadowRootMode` reflection. As I [pointed out at the time](https://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/5465#discussion_r1005976562), there's no developer-facing reason to need this. However, we did go through with renaming the attribute, with [significant work and ecosystem pain](https://groups.google.com/a/chromium.org/g/blink-dev/c/1n0MLr8G5NQ/m/ZcVvTd_vAgAJ) to migrate code to the new name, and deprecate the old name.\r\n\r\nGiven that we already went through all of that, I'd hope we wouldn't decide that now we don't need IDL reflections after all. And I'd hope we'd stick to one concept for all of the `<template>` attributes, meaning we keep all of the reflections such as `shadowRootClonable`.\r\n\r\nI.e. let's just keep the IDL reflections as we've spec'd them, please.",
